Optional: on this native path an out-of-range port (e.g. `-forward 10.0.0.1:65537`) still makes `net.Dial` fail with "invalid port" on every attempt, so the pre-bind loop spins forever. Validating once up front keeps per-attempt DNS:
```go
if _, p, err := net.SplitHostPort(*forward); err != nil {
	log.Fatalf("invalid forwarding target: %v", err)
} else if _, err := net.LookupPort("tcp", p); err != nil {
	log.Fatalf("invalid forwarding target: %v", err)
}
```

